WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.240
Is there any character that can seriously&nbsp;
challenge Roronoa Zoro's loyalty towards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:13.040
his captain Monkey D. Luffy? The first mate of&nbsp;
the straw hat pirates that stood side by side&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:18.960
with the future king of the pirates against the&nbsp;
strongest creature in the world. That was willing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:25.600
to sacrifice his life and dream at multiple&nbsp;
occasions. Swearing his allegiance and resolve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:32.480
to become the strongest swordsman in the world&nbsp;
to Luffy while almost bleeding to death. A man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:38.480
so powerful, that he was able to cut&nbsp;
Kaido, a feat that only Kozuki Oden,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:43.920
the strongest of the samurai of Wano was capable&nbsp;
of doing, and a user of conqueror's Haki,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:50.480
usually a sign that a person is meant to lead&nbsp;
and rule, and not follow another man. By the way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:56.560
not the only thing, that he has in common with&nbsp;
the dark king Silvers Rayleigh, another absolute&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:02.080
legend of the story, who was the right hand&nbsp;
man of Gol D. Roger, the first pirate king.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:08.320
So how is it, that Zoro is willing to&nbsp;
sacrifice so much for Luffy? To the point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:15.120
where his loyalty to his captain is an even more&nbsp;
respected and inspiring part of his character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:19.520
than his skills as a swordsman, his&nbsp;
discipline or his determination.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:23.440
I strongly believe, that Zoro is as&nbsp;
respectable and awesome as he is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:29.520
is due to his change and growth throughout&nbsp;
the story. If he had simply been loyal and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:35.120
trusting to Luffy right from the start,&nbsp;
it just wouldn't have had the same impact.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:41.760
Because when Luffy first meets and frees Zoro&nbsp;
and basically bribes him into joining his crew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:47.440
Zoro is very much a lone wolf type of&nbsp;
character, that hunts pirates on his own,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:53.120
following his own path. You can very&nbsp;
easily see why Zoro has the will of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.120 --> 00:02:00.160
a king and could have become a immensely powerful&nbsp;
leader on his own if he never had met Luffy.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:03.200
At the beginning of their journey,&nbsp;
I think it's fair to say, that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:09.760
Zoro sees joining Luffy as a useful step&nbsp;
towards reaching his goal of finding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:14.320
and defeating Mihawk and becoming&nbsp;
the strongest swordsman in the world.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:18.400
These are the five major moments in the&nbsp;
story that turned Zoro into one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:25.360
most, if not the most loyal and respectable&nbsp;
characters in all of anime and made him my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:28.560
personal favorite character in all of one piece.

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:35.200
Being completely humiliated and almost&nbsp;
killed by Mihawk at the Baratie. HIs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:40.240
objection to Usopp returning to the crew&nbsp;
on Water 7. His sacrifice on Thriller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:45.680
park. Swallowing his pride and begging to&nbsp;
train under Mihawk during the time skip.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:51.280
And pushing himself to the brink of&nbsp;
death during the raid on Onigashima.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:56.240
Getting to face off against Mihawk so&nbsp;
early into their journey, before even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:04.160
reaching the grand line was the best thing that&nbsp;
could have happened to Zoro. His humbling defeat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:11.120
against Mihawk changed his perspective on the&nbsp;
world. He was far from being the strongest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:18.640
but at the same time proved his potential and&nbsp;
more importantly his determination to us for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:26.160
the very first time. He would rather die for his&nbsp;
value of being an honourable swordsman, than run&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:32.720
away. Not only did he get recognised by Mihawk,&nbsp;
but more importantly, Luffy was not only more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:40.240
worried about his health than his skills, but&nbsp;
also shoed unwavering faith in Zoro's ambition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:46.800
and dream. Having seen Luffy risk his own&nbsp;
life for his friends a number of times now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:54.400
it changed Zoro's view and made him respect Luffy&nbsp;
for both his strength and his willingness to die&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.400 --> 00:04:00.240
for the right cause and values, remember the&nbsp;
two things that are most important to Zoro.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:06.480
This feeling of respect keeps on building&nbsp;
up, with Luffy saving Nami on Arlong park,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:12.720
reaching the grandline, freeing Drum island and&nbsp;
finally Alabasta from the rule of one of the seven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:19.040
warlords. Luffy has fully earned Zoro's respect&nbsp;
at this point, proving himself as powerful enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:25.680
to be his leader. Zoro is probably more aware&nbsp;
of the hierarchy and his position in the crew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:33.120
at this point that any other straw hat. Because&nbsp;
by accepting Luffy as his captain, LUffy also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:41.120
carries Zoro's personal pride and honor. So when&nbsp;
Usopp disrespects Luffy and wants to rejoin the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:49.600
crew without an apology, Zoro sees this insult to&nbsp;
Luffy as an insult to him personally. Discipline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:54.640
and respects towards those who are stronger than&nbsp;
you are the two major things he took away from his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.640 --> 00:05:00.240
Wano-training in Shimotsuke village, which we have&nbsp;
seen a lot in during the wano arc as well. I would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:07.760
say that Zoro is both right and wrong here at the&nbsp;
same time. He rightfully teaches Luffy a valuable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:14.160
lesson about being a good leader and warns him&nbsp;
that being a pirate isn't a game, a lesson that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:20.560
Luffy later has to learn the hard way by losing&nbsp;
his crew and failing to save his brother Ace.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:28.960
At the same time however, Zoro also hasn't fully&nbsp;
understood yet, what makes the straw hat crew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:34.960
so special. The fact, that everyone feels more&nbsp;
or less equal and is free to express who they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:40.560
are and what they think freely. Only during&nbsp;
their invasion of water seven, when he fights&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:46.800
together with Usopp and sees his determination and&nbsp;
willingness to fight and overcome his cowardice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:53.600
does Zoro understand how Usopp has felt and why&nbsp;
he left the crew in the first place. All while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.600 --> 00:06:01.200
Luffy is proving for the first time, that&nbsp;
he will do anything to get a member of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:06.640
straw hat family back. Even though Robin&nbsp;
also left the crew theoretically. Just as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:14.160
Luffy would do later with Sanji. So Zoro has&nbsp;
now become a very important anchor for Luffy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:19.280
teaching him to take things seriously and become&nbsp;
a better leader overall, while at the same time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:24.800
learning to appreciate the love and care the crew&nbsp;
has for each other. That is actually something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:32.320
I feel some people tend to overlook here, and&nbsp;
just another reason that makes Zoro so awesome.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:38.720
Literally Taking on all of Luffy's pain without&nbsp;
so much as a second of hesitation on Thriller Bark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:47.600
then is probably still my favorite moment in the&nbsp;
entire story up to this point. It's just argh. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:54.560
much raw emotion. Like legit, whenever you feel&nbsp;
like you need a good cry, just rewatch this scene.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.560 --> 00:07:01.200
In case you forgot, Zoro is already pretty much&nbsp;
unable to stand up himself, when he blocks Kuma's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:08.000
path to an unconscious Luffy. He bargains for him&nbsp;
to let Luffy go in exchange for his own life. Kuma&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:16.960
takes him up on that offer and using his unique&nbsp;
devil fruit powers extracts all of the damage and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:24.480
pain that Luffy has accumulated during his fight&nbsp;
and gives Zoro a small taste of it, which brings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:31.520
him to his knees. He then lets him know that&nbsp;
taking in the rest will kill him. Quick side note,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:37.840
since Kuma was actually not an enemy, I suppose&nbsp;
he made sure that Zoro would not actually die,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:45.200
but he didn't exactly hold back either. Zoro does&nbsp;
not know this of course. And yet, without so much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:54.800
as a moment of hesitation, he steps right into the&nbsp;
bubble. Which leads to this most epic moment of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.800 --> 00:08:01.120
all time, where Sanji finds him standing there,&nbsp;
bleeding, telling him that nothing happened.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:07.760
Now this is of course the ultimate sacrifice he is&nbsp;
willing to make there for luffy. He puts the dream&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:14.560
of his captain and the way he is able to change&nbsp;
the world above his own dream. Zoro has completely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:20.000
left behind the idea that Luffy is merely a&nbsp;
stepping stone for himself. Luffy's dream is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:28.480
now also his dream. But it gets even crazier.&nbsp;
Remember how Zoro knocked out Sanji, who was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:37.360
willing to sacrifice himself as well? Zoro not&nbsp;
only is prepared to give his life for Luffy, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:45.200
for every single member of the crew. Including of&nbsp;
course Sanji, despite all their brawls. It shows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:52.160
that Zoro has at this point fully internalised&nbsp;
that the straw hats are not only a crew, but a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.160 --> 00:09:00.960
family. And as Luffy's right hand man, it's his&nbsp;
responsibility to step in and give his everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:08.480
to protect the crew as a whole. The crew has&nbsp;
become the most valuable thing in his life now.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:15.200
But it gets even crazier when Zoro is sent to&nbsp;
Mohawks island after Sabaody. Because after seeing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:21.520
that Luffy lost ace during the war, he throws away&nbsp;
his honor and begs Mihawk to train him. At first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:28.480
Mihawk is absolutely disgusted about this. He&nbsp;
thinks that Zoro is simply too weak to leave the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:34.640
island on his own and that he has lost all pride&nbsp;
as a swordsman. Only when he finds out that Zoro&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:41.600
defeated all the mandrills and decided to&nbsp;
stay behind anyways, does he see the truth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:47.680
Zoro has made Luffy's dream part of his own.&nbsp;
He wants to make LUffy the king of the pirates.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:56.400
He wants to be strong enough to help his captain&nbsp;
get there and protect his crew from ever having to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.400 --> 00:10:02.080
suffer through something like on Sabaody again.&nbsp;
He is willing to throw away his personal honour&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:09.280
as a swordsman, because his honor as the&nbsp;
vice captain of the straw hat crew is now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:14.800
more important to him. I have made an&nbsp;
entire video about Mihawk explaining his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:20.080
crazy character development during and after the&nbsp;
war, if you want the whole story. But in short,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:26.480
Mihawk has learned Luffy's crazy power&nbsp;
and potential during Marineford, a man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:32.000
who got the respect of both shanks&nbsp;
and whitebeard, and thus ends up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:41.280
training Zoro and acknowledging him as a worthy&nbsp;
swordsman. Mihawk sees how much Zoro has grown.

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:50.640
Not only does it turn Zoro into one of the&nbsp;
strongest people in One pIece, but also earns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:58.240
him a crazy bounty of 320.000.000 berries.&nbsp;
Which I'm honestly really jealous of. I have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:05.440
580.000 subscribers, which if it were $ and&nbsp;
converted to Berries, would be a 58.000.000 berry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:14.400
bounty. For comparison, even Trebol, a man that&nbsp;
consists of 99% slime has a bounty of 99.000.000.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:20.880
So please help me overtake Trebol by subscribing&nbsp;
to the channel and raising my bounty.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:29.200
Which brings us all the way to Wano, an arc&nbsp;
that coincidentally mirrors a lot of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:34.800
events during Thriller bark. So it might or&nbsp;
might not have been surprising to find out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:40.720
that Zoro once again has pushed himself across his&nbsp;
limits for Luffy and his crew. He has faced off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:47.120
face to face with Kaido himself, side by side&nbsp;
with his captain, something we all wanted to see,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:53.440
and dealt some real damage to the YOnko,&nbsp;
earning his respect and revealing his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:59.760
conquerors haki to us, still one of the most&nbsp;
hype moments of the entire raid. and after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:06.800
taking some heavy damage in the process, once&nbsp;
again did not hesitate for even a second to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:11.840
the wonder drug of the minks that would come&nbsp;
with devastating consequences for his health.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:18.800
Without batting an eyelash though, Zoro&nbsp;
took it and went off to take down King,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:24.400
Kaido's number two in command and one of the&nbsp;
most powerful characters in the entire story.

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:36.880
And once again, Zoro has now been pushed to&nbsp;
the brink of death, where he actually saw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:40.560
death himself with his cloak&nbsp;
and his scythe, though who knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:42.800
what that might actually be all about in the end.

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:49.760
However, if you want to dive even deeper into&nbsp;
Zoro's fantastic character arc and the fantastic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:53.520
secret how he convinced his biggest rival Mihawk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:57.520
to become his mentor, you really&nbsp;
can't ignore this video right here.

